# Goblin Gold

> The design overview: what the game is and what it's trying to be. Demo Game is the sandbox Game Studio is
> developed against, so this game stays deliberately small: big enough to show every studio module working
> together, small enough to change in an afternoon.

## Pitch
A small goblin wanders a mossy clearing looking for treasure. Walk up to a chest, open it, and celebrate the
gold inside. Find every chest to win.

## Pillars
- **Readable at a glance.** Chunky, stylised models and a calm palette; the goblin is always the clearest thing on screen.
- **Every action has a reaction.** Walking animates, chests creak open, the goblin waves when it finds gold.
- **Made in the studio.** Every asset comes from a Game Studio module (models from 3D Models, code from Game
  Code sessions), so the game doubles as a showcase of the pipeline.

## Core loop
1. Explore the clearing with **WASD** (hold the right mouse button and drag to turn the camera, wheel to zoom).
2. Near a closed chest, press **E** to open it: the lid swings open, gold is added to the counter and the goblin waves.
3. When every chest is open, the clearing is cleared.

## World
| Thing | Model | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Goblin (player) | `assets/models/goblin` | 1.1 m tall, rigged; clips `idle`, `walk`, `wave` |
| Treasure chest | `assets/models/chest` | 0.6 m; hinge rig with `open`/`close` clips; holds gold |
| Barrel | `assets/models/barrel` | 0.9 m scenery, solid |
| Boulder | `assets/models/rock` | 0.7 m mossy scenery, solid |

The clearing is `assets/scenes/clearing.json`: a grassy ground, four chests, and barrels and boulders placed
as landmarks. Each kind of thing is a prefab in `assets/prefabs/`.

## Music
| Piece | Score | Where it plays |
|---|---|---|
| Goblin Gold | `assets/music/goblin-gold/song.json` | The whole game, looping: D dorian, 104 bpm, flute and clarinet over pizzicato strings, about a minute |
| Treasure Found | `assets/music/treasure-found/song.json` | Once, when a chest opens: a glockenspiel flourish ending on D major |

## Scope
Single player, one scene, a few minutes of play. Deliberately left out: enemies, inventory, saving, sound effects (until the SFX module exists), menus beyond a "cleared" banner.
package game

import "core:math/linalg"
import "engine:engine"
import "engine:input"

OPEN_REACH :: 1.4 // metres from the goblin to a chest's centre

// Finds the nearest closed chest in reach; E opens it, adds its gold and makes the goblin wave.
update_chests :: proc() {
	here := engine.world_position(game.player)
	game.near = 0
	best := f32(OPEN_REACH)
	ents, chests := engine.view(Chest)
	for c, i in chests {
		if c.open do continue
		d := linalg.length((engine.world_position(ents[i]) - here).xz)
		if d < best do best, game.near = d, ents[i]
	}
	if game.near != 0 && input.action_pressed("interact") do open_chest(game.near)
}

open_chest :: proc(e: Entity) {
	c := engine.get(e, Chest)
	if c == nil || c.open do return
	c.open = true
	game.gold += c.gold
	engine.play_animation(e, "open", once = true)
	engine.play_sound_at("sounds/chest-open/chest-open.ogg", engine.world_position(e))
	game.gold_in, game.gold_at = 0.5, engine.world_position(e)
	engine.play_sound(JINGLE_TREASURE, volume = 0.9, bus = .Music)
	// Face the chest while celebrating.
	if t := engine.get(game.player, engine.Transform); t != nil {
		to := engine.world_position(e) - engine.world_position(game.player)
		to.y = 0
		if linalg.length(to) > 0.01 do t.rotation = engine.look_rotation(to)
	}
	celebrate()
}

chests_left :: proc() -> (left, total: int) {
	_, chests := engine.view(Chest)
	for c in chests {
		total += 1
		if !c.open do left += 1
	}
	return
}

// The coins jingle half a second after the lid starts to open.
update_gold_sound :: proc(dt: f32) {
	if game.gold_in <= 0 do return
	game.gold_in -= dt
	if game.gold_in <= 0 do engine.play_sound_at("sounds/gold/gold.ogg", game.gold_at, volume = 0.7)
}
package game

import "core:fmt"
import "engine:ui"

draw_ui :: proc() {
	left, total := chests_left()

	r := ui.anchor(.Top_Left, 230, 76, {16, 16})
	ui.panel(r)
	col := ui.column(ui.inset(r, 12), 26, 2)
	ui.label(ui.next(&col), fmt.tprintf("Gold: %d", game.gold), size = 26)
	ui.label(ui.next(&col), fmt.tprintf("Chests: %d / %d opened", total - left, total), color = ui.theme().text_dim)

	if game.near != 0 {
		p := ui.anchor(.Bottom, 260, 44, {0, 60})
		ui.panel(p)
		ui.label(p, "E  Open the chest", .Center)
	}
	if total > 0 && left == 0 {
		b := ui.anchor(.Top, 520, 70, {0, 40})
		ui.panel(b)
		ui.label(b, "The clearing is cleared!", .Center, 34)
	}
	hint := ui.anchor(.Bottom_Right, 330, 30, {16, 12})
	ui.label(hint, "WASD walk   |   right-drag look   |   wheel zoom", .Right, 16, ui.theme().text_dim)
}
